    {# Purpose #}
    <section class="section" id="purpose">
      <div class="conteneur">
        <div class="association-rail">
        <h2>Our purpose</h2>
        <figure class="bloc-amcf association-statuts">
          <blockquote>
            <p>
              The purpose of the association is to contribute to the modernization of the French keyboard and to make
              written input easier (accented capitals, typography, symbols, accessibility, digital practices) through
              free and open-source keyboard layouts that install on Windows, macOS and Linux.
            </p>
          </blockquote>
          <figcaption>Article 2 of the statutes, signed on 17&nbsp;March 2026. Translated from French; the French text is the only legally binding version.</figcaption>
        </figure>
        <p>In particular, it may:</p>
        <ul class="association-liste">
          <li>develop, maintain and distribute keyboard layouts suited to contemporary use;</li>
          <li>distribute educational and technical resources;</li>
          <li>run awareness activities, workshops and sessions in schools and companies;</li>
          <li>work with researchers and institutions to evaluate the benefits of these layouts
            scientifically;</li>
          <li>seek grants, donations and partnerships compatible with its purpose.</li>
        </ul>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    {# Activities #}
    <section class="section" id="activities">
      <div class="conteneur">
        <div class="association-rail">
        <h2>What the association has done</h2>
        <p class="association-chapo">Its activities since it was founded, in March 2026.</p>
        <div class="association-activites">
          <div class="association-activite">
            <h3>Publishing and distributing the layout</h3>
            <p>
              The association publishes the AZERTY Global layout for Windows, macOS and Linux, free of charge and
              under the open-source EUPL&nbsp;1.2 license. On Windows, a dedicated app is published on the Microsoft Store. The
              <a href="https://github.com/AMCF-asso">source code</a> is
              public and the layout remains a <a href="/en/download">free download</a>.
            </p>
          </div>
          <div class="association-activite">
            <h3>Equipping organizations</h3>
            <p>
              An <a href="/en/download">enterprise kit</a> is available for IT departments: an MSIX package signed by
              the association, a deployment sheet and printable materials. Dedicated pages answer the questions
              of <a href="/entreprises" hreflang="fr">companies<span class="visuellement-cache"> (in French)</span></a> and <a href="/ecoles" hreflang="fr">schools<span class="visuellement-cache"> (in French)</span></a>.
            </p>
          </div>
          <div class="association-activite">
            <h3>Publishing educational resources</h3>
            <p>
              The site gathers free resources: a <a href="/en/guide">quick-start guide</a>,
              a <a href="/en/french-typography">French typography guide</a>,
              a <a href="/en/comparison">comparison of layouts</a>,
              a <a href="/en/azerty-history">history of AZERTY</a> and a
              <a href="/en/faq">FAQ</a>.
            </p>
          </div>
          <div class="association-activite">
            <h3>Running the community</h3>
            <p>
              User feedback comes in through
              <a href="https://github.com/AMCF-asso">GitHub</a> and an open
              <a href="https://discord.gg/nYknqshJz3">Discord server</a>.
              It shapes later versions. Report a bug or a suggestion from the
              <a href="/en/contact">Contact us</a> page.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="association-reperes">
        <h3>Milestones</h3>
        <ul class="association-liste">
          <li><strong>17&nbsp;March 2026</strong>: founding general meeting in Clermont-Ferrand,
            statutes signed.</li>
          <li><strong>27&nbsp;March 2026</strong>: receipt of the declaration of creation issued by the
            Riom sub-prefecture.</li>
          <li><strong>7&nbsp;April 2026</strong>: published in the <em lang="fr">Journal officiel des associations</em>,
            announcement no.&nbsp;1771.</li>
          <li><strong>15&nbsp;June 2026</strong>: final version of AZERTY Global, published under the
            EUPL&nbsp;1.2 license for Windows, macOS and Linux; Windows app 1.0.0 on the Microsoft Store
            on 29&nbsp;June.</li>
          <li><strong>2026</strong>: free educational resources put online:
            <a href="/en/guide">quick-start guide</a>, <a href="/en/french-typography">French typography
            guide</a>, <a href="/en/comparison">comparison of layouts</a> and
            <a href="/en/azerty-history">history of AZERTY</a>.</li>
        </ul>
        </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

